# Star Fort - a new island of the library, seven times the size (x7)
# A great star-shaped fortress on a desert table-land: four bastions round a parade ground, a keep with a great gun on its
# roof, a powder magazine in a pit beside it. Governor Ines Albrecht held Fort Meridian through eleven seasons of the Siege
# of the Beasts; the garrison is gone, and the island's beasts still come over the walls, bastion by bastion, their
# leader last.
# Quest "Hold the Fort" (25 steps in 4 chapters): the gate (the ramp, the governor's order, the gate key, the parade, the
# first wave), the bastions (north, east, west and south - a wave of a different beast and a commander's locker each),
# the magazine (the four keys, the gunner's chart, three kegs - one in the flooded sea-cave store - and the shot), the
# last stand (the great gun, the pack's leader at the gate, the governor's journal and chest).
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe star_fort) through the editor's own operations.
include lib_selene
include lib_rt
include lib_sea
include lib_features
new
# (nature: desert, Like Raft - acacias, cacti and scrub on the slopes and round the fort; the fort's ground cleared)
gen Trees=0.38 Bushes=0.5 Rocks=0.55 Harvest=0.25 BeachThings=0.3
gen Seed=9222 Radius=119 Height=28 Roughness=0.35 Peaks=1 Shape=4 Style=2 BeachWidth=0.4 Cliffs=0.75 PeakShape=0.3
gen Water=0.5 SeaRocks=0.3 SeaFinds=0.3 Sunken=0.4 Hostiles=0 Friendly=0 SeaLife=0
generate

# ===== THE LAND ===========================================================================================================
# The plateau (the map, seed 9222): flat at 28 m over x -65..70, z -65..65, steep red cliffs all round to a low shore. The
# fort on it round 5 0: banks 4 m high (32 m) in a four-pointed star - the bastions' points N 5 45, E 50 0, S 5 -45, W -40 0,
# the curtains' inner corners at 23/-13 x 18/-18 - the gate in the south-east corner (23 -18), the keep in the middle
# (2..8 x -4.5..4.5, three storeys and the gun on its roof), the magazine in a pit beside it (-8..-2 x -4.5..4.5, 24.5 m).
# The ramp road from the gate cut down the south-east cliff to the guardhouse at 89 -42 and the landing at 106 -50; the
# sea-cave store (flooded, 5 m down) at the south cliff's foot, 5 -84.

# --- Terrain: the banks (strokes along the star, the gate's gap left open), the bastions' tops, the ramps up to them from
# the parade ground; the magazine's pit; the ramp road in two legs; the guardhouse's yard; the sea-cave store's pool --------
brush flatten from 5 45 to 23 18 r=3 s=20 frames=300 h=32
brush flatten from 23 18 to 50 0 r=3 s=20 frames=300 h=32
brush flatten from 50 0 to 27.16 -15.23 r=3 s=20 frames=300 h=32
brush flatten from 20.23 -22.16 to 5 -45 r=3 s=20 frames=300 h=32
brush flatten from 5 -45 to -13 -18 r=3 s=20 frames=300 h=32
brush flatten from -13 -18 to -40 0 r=3 s=20 frames=300 h=32
brush flatten from -40 0 to -13 18 r=3 s=20 frames=300 h=32
brush flatten from -13 18 to 5 45 r=3 s=20 frames=300 h=32
brush flatten at 5 42 r=7 s=20 frames=300 h=32
for i 0 8 1
brush flatten at {5+0*$i} {27+1.12*$i} r=2.5 s=20 frames=150 h={28+0.5*$i}
next
brush flatten at 47 0 r=7 s=20 frames=300 h=32
for i 0 8 1
brush flatten at {32+1.12*$i} {0+0*$i} r=2.5 s=20 frames=150 h={28+0.5*$i}
next
brush flatten at 5 -42 r=7 s=20 frames=300 h=32
for i 0 8 1
brush flatten at {5+0*$i} {-27+-1.12*$i} r=2.5 s=20 frames=150 h={28+0.5*$i}
next
brush flatten at -37 0 r=7 s=20 frames=300 h=32
for i 0 8 1
brush flatten at {-22+-1.12*$i} {0+0*$i} r=2.5 s=20 frames=150 h={28+0.5*$i}
next
brush flatten from -5 -3 to -5 3 r=5 s=20 frames=400 h=24.5
for i 0 10 1
brush flatten at {27+2.8*$i} {-21-2.4*$i} r=3 s=20 frames=150 h={28-1.4*$i}
next
for i 0 10 1
brush flatten at {55+2.6*$i} {-45-0.3*$i} r=3 s=20 frames=150 h={14-1.1*$i}
next
