scatter "Pickup_Landmark_PineappleLandmark" 6 at 0 0 r=83.3 seed=4300 free=3

# --- Raft's story machinery (lib_features; the user, 2026-10-06: every Raft feature on at least one island): the
# quartermaster kept the north barracks as his strongroom behind one of Tangaroa's keycard doors (in its doorway at -16 9,
# the floor 28.05 m) - his keycard dropped out on the glacis; a hatch on the parade ground over the garrison's hidden stores
call keydoor x=-16 z=8.72 h=28.05 yaw=90 alias=qmdoor vault=qmvault vx=-18 vz=7.2 vh=28.05 vyaw=270 items=TradeToken*6;MetalIngot*3;Bolt*4 kx=40 kz=36 kr=14 seed=3101 keychest=qmsatchel keytitle="Quartermaster's satchel" keyitems=Rope*2;Leather*1
call hatchcache x=14 z=8 r=5 seed=3102 alias=storehatch chest=storehatchchest items=Cooked_GenericMeat*3;PlasticBottle_Water*2;Rope*2
# --- Raft's finds in the shallows round the island (lib_sea; keep this after the terrain and building lines) ------------
call shallows r=139 deep=5 n=2

# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (25 steps, 4 chapters) =============================================
info title=Star Fort
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A great star-shaped fortress on a desert table-land, its garrison gone and its walls still besieged by the island's beasts, bastion by bastion. Take the commanders' keys, open the magazine, fire the great gun - and meet the pack's leader at the gate.
island on.arrive=message||A red table-land with a fortress on top shaped like a star, a gun on its keep, flags still on the gatehouse. Something howls on the north wall.

story gatekey|Fort gate key|quest:Utopia_KeyEntrance|The fort gate's great iron key.
story bastionkey|Bastion key|quest:Caravan_KeyMayor|A commander's key, one of the four that open the magazine.
story powder|Keg of powder|quest:Vasagatan_GasTank|A small keg of dry gunpowder, its bung sealed with wax.
story shot|Great gun's shot|quest:Vasagatan_Bullet|An iron ball as big as your head.

note order The governor's last order | FORT MERIDIAN - LAST ORDER OF THE GOVERNOR\n\nThe relief ship is here. All hands aboard. I will follow tomorrow.\n\nTo whoever holds this fort after us: the beasts come over the bastions one after another, as they have every season - north, east, west, then up from the south sea caves. Each commander's key is in his locker on his bastion. The four keys open the magazine under the keep.\nThree kegs and a shot fire the great gun. The gun always brings their leader up the ramp. When it falls, the siege is over for the year.\n\nGate key: the guardhouse below.\n- I. Albrecht, Governor
note guardchest Guardhouse chest | The guard's chest: a lantern, a coil of rope, his dinner - and the fort gate's great iron key.
loot guardchest story:gatekey*1;Rope*2;Cooked_GenericMeat*1
prop guardchest loot.refill=0
note northlocker North commander's locker | The north commander's locker: his telescope, a letter home never sent - and the first bastion key.
loot northlocker story:bastionkey*1;Glass*1
prop northlocker loot.refill=0
note eastlocker East commander's locker | The east commander's locker: boar tusks nailed inside the door, a tin of tobacco - and the second bastion key.
loot eastlocker story:bastionkey*1;Leather*1
prop eastlocker loot.refill=0
note westlocker West commander's locker | The west commander's locker: feathers, a sling, a list of screechers shot (forty-one) - and the third key.
loot westlocker story:bastionkey*1;Feather*3
prop westlocker loot.refill=0
note southlocker South commander's locker | The south commander's locker, damp from the sea: a scarab shell as big as a plate - and the fourth key.
loot southlocker story:bastionkey*1;Scrap*2
prop southlocker loot.refill=0
note gunnerchart The master gunner's chart | THE GREAT GUN - LOADING\n\nThree kegs of powder. Dry ones on the top rack - two left. The third dry keg is sealed in a cask in the sea-cave store under the south cliff (flooded since the spring tide - hold your breath, there's air under its ceiling). Down the ramp road and round under the cliff.\nOne shot from the pile.\nLoad on the keep's roof, fire, and stand by the gate.
note journal The governor's journal | (on the governor's desk, open at the last page)\n\nEleven seasons. Eleven times the pack came over the walls, eleven times their leader came up the ramp when the gun spoke, eleven times we held.\n\nThey are not cruel. They are hungry, and this was their island first.\n\nIf you held it once - the chest is yours. Then leave the gate open when you go. Let them have it for a season.\n- Ines
note governorchest The governor's chest | Governor Albrecht's chest: the fort's pay chest, titanium from the gun foundry, the plans for the battery charger that ran the signal lamps, her sword, and dried dates.
loot governorchest TradeToken*15;TitaniumIngot*4;Blueprint_BatteryCharger*1;Sword_Titanium*1;Cooked_GenericMeat*3
prop governorchest loot.refill=0
note barracksbox Barracks box | A soldier's box under a bunk: socks, dice, a letter, rope.
loot barracksbox Rope*3;Wool*1;Plank*3
prop barracksbox loot.refill=0
note cookbarrel Cook house barrel | The cook house barrel: flour gone to stone, but tins and water that kept.
loot cookbarrel Cooked_GenericMeat*2;PlasticBottle_Water*2;Raw_Potato*2
prop cookbarrel loot.refill=0
note sunkbarrel Sunk powder barrel | A barrel that went off the jetty: the powder ruined, the iron hoops good.
loot sunkbarrel MetalOre*2;Scrap*3;Bolt*2
prop sunkbarrel loot.refill=0
note outworkbox Outwork box | A box in the ruined outwork on the glacis: an old sentry's things.
loot outworkbox Nail*8;Stone*3;Rope*2
prop outworkbox loot.refill=0

prop gatelock obj.name=gatelock
prop gatelock beh.use=Unlock the fort gate
prop gatelock if.use=has|story:gatekey|1\nstate|fortgate|closed
prop gatelock on.use=message||The great key grinds round. The bamboo gate sinks into the ground with a roar of dust.\nopen|fortgate\nsound||event:/exploring/utopia/door_entrance_open
prop gatelock else.use=message||The fort gate's lock. The governor's order says where the key is.
